 "internal_silences": [],
 "text": "When I moved into my first home, I could not cook at all. I ate the same simple meals, and I spent too much on takeaway food. So I made a plan. Every Sunday, I would learn one new dish. I started with soup, because it is hard to get wrong. Then I tried rice, eggs and baked vegetables. Some meals were good, and some were not. But each week, I became a little faster and a little more relaxed in the kitchen. After a few months, I could cook for friends. My advice is simple. Start with one dish, and give yourself time to practise. Cooking soon becomes fun."
